1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,000
This is equipe: a squad of AI coding agents that works like a team —

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
a PM, engineers, a board of tickets, and you accepting the work.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Every member here runs on an NVIDIA Nemotron model on Nebius Token Factory —

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,000
no other AI subscription, just a Nebius key and the open-source Codex CLI as the agent loop.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
I ask the PM for a small change; it writes a ticket and hands it to an engineer.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Nemotron decides what to do and Codex's tools do it, in the engineer's own git worktree:

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
it writes the code, runs the tests in a sandbox, and hands the work in.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
My checkout is never touched.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Then a second Nemotron call reviews the hand-in.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:16,000
It reads the diff against the ticket and comes back with a verdict, a short summary,

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,000
risks with the file and line, and the tests the change is missing —

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
in my language.

13
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:41,000
It's advice, not authority: the review goes on the ticket's record, and I still decide —

14
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:50,000
here I send it back with the risk it found.

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Everything is on the record: equipe review lists the account's Nemotron models

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:08,000
and reviews any repository's changes,

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
and the daemon logs each member turn's Token Factory request ids and tokens.

18
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Under the hood, members run Codex's agent with Token Factory's Responses API as its provider,

19
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
through a small relay that keeps every tool a plain function.

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The key stays in the environment and never reaches the logs.

21
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
equipe is open source under MIT.

22
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
A whole team of agents, running on NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius.
